{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNW","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNW","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaGeneral","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTListCorner","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTCornerListConnection","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWRatio"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L199-L203","doc":"**The general Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook-length formula `#SYT(λ) = dimHLF λ` (sorry-free).**\nCanonical name; the corpus' general-`n` HLF, closed via the GNW corner recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimAitkenIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimAitkenIdentity","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L193-L197","doc":"**The general-`n` Aitken/Frobenius determinant identity (sorry-free).** Canonical name; closes the\nformer determinant-blocked gap via the GNW corner recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimAitkenIdentity_of_gnw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimAitkenIdentity_of_gnw","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L174-L183","doc":"**The Aitken/Frobenius determinant identity, via the GNW route (sorry-free).**  Once the\ndeterminant-blocked residual gap (`det(1/(β_i − k + j)!)`, needing Specht/RSK infra absent from the\npinned Mathlib), here obtained with **no determinant infrastructure**: combine the divisor-free HLF\n`#SYT·∏h = n!` with the merged hook-product identity (i) `∏h · betaProdGap = betaFactProd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF_gnw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF_gnw","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L164-L172","doc":"**General Frame–Robinson–Thrall HLF `#SYT(λ) = dimHLF λ`** via the GNW route (sorry-free).\nRouted through the self-contained corner recursion rather than any Mathlib determinant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_mul_prodHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_mul_prodHooks","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L151-L162","doc":"**Divisor-free HLF `#SYT(λ) · ∏h_λ = n!`** (over `ℕ`) — conditional on the two GNW identities.\nThis is exactly the divisor-free Frame–Robinson–Thrall form; proving the two GNW identities makes it\nunconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_factorial_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_factorial_div","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L145-L149","doc":"**#SYT(λ) = n!/∏h_λ over `ℚ`** — conditional on `cornerRecursion` + `gnwHookIdentity`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.gnwHookIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.gnwHookIdentity","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L56-L76","doc":"**(GNW hook) hook-summation identity — the sole remaining gap of the GNW route.**  Summing the\nhook-product ratios over the removable corners gives the cell count: `∑_{corners c} ∏h_λ / ∏h_{λ∖c} = n`.\nThis is the partial-fractions / telescoping core of the Greene–Nijenhuis–Wilf proof — the rational\nidentity that turns the count recursion into the hook-length formula.\n\n**Closure (PROVED, sorry-free).**  Via the *already-proved* β-number identity (i)\n(`SYTHookFormulaGeneral.prodHooks_mul_betaProdGap`: `∏h_λ · betaProdGap = betaFactProd`,\n`β_i = λ_i + (k−1−i)`), each ratio rewrites as a β-ratio, reducing this to the **β-Lagrange identity**\n\n    ∑_i β_i · ∏_{j≠i} (β_i − 1 − β_j) / (β_i − β_j) = (∑_i β_i) − C(k,2)   ( = sz l ),\n\na self-contained `ℚ` partial-fractions identity over the distinct `β_i` (non-corner `i` drop out because\n`β_i − 1 = β_{i+1}` there).  The β-Lagrange identity is proved in `SYTBetaLagrange.betaLagrange` via the\nVandermonde/`det_vandermonde` keystone (`SYTVandermonde.interp_leadingCoeff`); the per-corner hook ratio\n(`SYTHookGNWRatio.prodHooks_ratio`/`prodHooks_removeCorner`, incl. the row-drop corner) and the assembly\nover corners (`SYTHookGNWRatio.gnwHookIdentity_proof`) discharge this identity outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.cornerRecursion","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNW.lean#L44-L54","doc":"**(GNW count) corner recursion of the standard-tableau count (proved).**  In any standard tableau of\nshape `λ` the largest entry `n` occupies a removable corner; deleting it is a bijection\n`SYT(λ) ≃ ⨆_{corners c} SYT(λ ∖ c)`, whence the count splits as a sum.  Proved sorry-free in\n`SYTCornerListConnection.cornerRecursion_proof` via the structural branching rule. ","signatureChunk":0}]}